      "message": "If I have understood correctly, someone calling SFLOWPS_set_attr(), like this:\nhttps://github.com/FDio/vpp/blob/98b1c75b3103857757c0b92ce6290b8a4ec24836/src/plugins/sflow/sflow.c#L344\nwould risk having 1-3 bytes copied into the netlink attribute padding from beyond the end of the value?\n\n(If so, I wonder why Coverity didn\u0027t complain at the time. Perhaps it was satisfied that the buffers being submitted were all at least quad-aligned by the allocator.)\n\nDoes the fix ensure that the pad bytes, if required, are always set to 0?  I don\u0027t remember, but I suspect that this was the reason for the iovec included the pad bytes in the first place.  Did not want to leave any bytes in the message buffer unset.",
